      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `withRadix(-1)` (the `DEFAULT_RADIX` sentinel) on a freshly-constructed `Value` returns the same instance, because the radix hasn't changed. I'll rewrite it with a descriptive name, clear constant usage, and a comment explaining the identity-return contract.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces the cryptic magic number `-1` with `JsonFormat.DEFAULT_RADIX`, renames the method to `test_withRadix_returnsThisWhenRadixUnchanged`, uses meaningful variable names, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the identity short-circuit contract being verified."
